title: CoachSharma_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic CoachSharma>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

After hearing about the prestigious sports academy, Raju walks the long distance to the facility.

He knows he doesn't belong there and can't afford the fees.

But his hunger to learn proper techniques drives him forward.

The imposing gates of the sports academy loom before him.

Manicured grounds and professional equipment represent everything he aspires to but cannot access.

The contrast weighs heavily on his shoulders.

Yet his determination propels him forward despite the risk of rejection.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Furious">>
Coach Sharma: Hey! You there, boy!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Furious">>
Coach Sharma: Who let you into this academy?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: These grounds are private property!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: Not a playground for stray kids from the slums!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: Sir, I'm sorry for disturbing practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: I only wanted to watch and maybe learn something.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I've been practicing cricket with my brother.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Disappointed">>
Raju: But I know I need proper coaching to really improve.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Disgusted">>
Coach Sharma: Learn? Ha!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: You think watching from the sidelines will magically make you a cricketer?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Boy, cricket isn't a game you learn by osmosis.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: You need fees - substantial fees.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: You need proper equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: You need years of disciplined training under professional guidance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Irritated">>
Coach Sharma: These boys pay fifteen thousand rupees per month for coaching.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: They've been training for years.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: They have everything cricket requires.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Resources, commitment, family support.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: You have none of that.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: Go back to your galli cricket with tennis balls and wooden sticks.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Disgusted">>
Coach Sharma: That's your level.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Maybe I don't have money or fancy equipment now, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: But one day I'll prove to you that I can play cricket properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: One day you'll see that talent and determination matter more than fees.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: Dreams are cheap, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Anyone can dream of playing cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: But discipline is costly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: It costs time, money, sacrifice, and commitment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Irritated">>
Coach Sharma: Until you understand that difference, you're wasting both my time and yours.



<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju walks away, Coach Sharma's harsh words echo in his mind.

He feels the familiar sting of rejection based on economic circumstances rather than ability.

Yet beneath the hurt lies a burning determination.

Someday he will return to demonstrate that passion and persistence can overcome barriers.

<<set $CoachSharma_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===
title: CoachSharma_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic CoachSharma>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

Despite yesterday's harsh dismissal, Raju returns to the prestigious sports academy.

His resolve is strengthened rather than weakened by yesterday's confrontation.

The academy grounds stretch out before him.

The pristine facility represents both the pinnacle of cricket training and the embodiment of social barriers.

Yet his hunger for genuine improvement compels him to return.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Astonished">>
Coach Sharma: You again?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Irritated">>
Coach Sharma: Didn't I make myself clear yesterday?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: Why do you persist in wasting your time here?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: This academy is for serious students with serious commitments.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma"  "Angry">>
Coach Sharma: Not for curiosity seekers who don't belong.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Because I want to learn, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I understand that I can't afford to train here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: And I know I don't have the proper equipment or background.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: But even if I'm not allowed to play, I can still listen.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I can still observe.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Discipline means showing up consistently, doesn't it?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Astonished">>
Coach Sharma: Discipline?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: That's a big word for someone your age.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: Most of my own paying trainees don't even understand what real discipline means.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Disappointed">>
Coach Sharma: Children whose families invest thousands of rupees monthly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: These boys have every advantage.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Proper equipment, dedicated practice time, nutritional support, family backing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Irritated">>
Coach Sharma: Yet half of them complain about early training sessions.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Disgusted">>
Coach Sharma: They make excuses about difficult drills.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Disappointed">>
Coach Sharma: They give up when progress becomes challenging.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Then they don't really understand what they have, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Discipline means doing the hard work especially when no one believes in you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: When you have no guarantees, when every door seems closed.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: It means showing up because improvement matters more than comfort.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: Hmm.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: And you believe you possess this kind of discipline?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: You think you understand what serious cricket training requires?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: How do you plan to prove this discipline to me, boy?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: Words are easy when there's no real test behind them.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<AutoAdvance true>>
Make a Choice
<<AutoAdvance false>>

