title: CoachSharma_Day4
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic CoachSharma>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

After proving his dedication through consistent work, Raju hopes for the chance to demonstrate his actual cricket ability.

The academy nets beckon tantalizingly as Raju completes another session of preparation work.

His hands are eager to grip a proper cricket bat after days of proving his character through unglamorous labor.

Coach Sharma's presence carries a different energy today.

The period of testing commitment through routine tasks may be giving way to evaluation of actual cricket potential.

Though Raju understands that earning this opportunity required first demonstrating reliability and dedication.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Alright, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Neutral">>
Coach Sharma: You've proven you can work without complaint and show up consistently.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Now comes the real test.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: Show me what you can actually do with a cricket bat.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: Really, sir?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: You'll actually let me bat in the professional nets?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Don't get ahead of yourself, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: This isn't a training session - it's purely assessment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: I'm going to bowl ten deliveries at you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Neutral">>
Coach Sharma: We'll see what you can do with proper equipment under controlled conditions.

// The first delivery reveals raw talent struggling with technical flaws but producing moments of brilliance.
<<HideAllCharacters>>
Coach Sharma watches in awe as Raju Handles all the balls properly, playing each ball on its merit.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Astonished">>
Coach Sharma: Interesting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: Again.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Skeptical">>
Coach Sharma: Raw talent, definitely.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Smiling">>
Coach Sharma: Natural timing that can't be taught.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: But your technique is absolutely terrible.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Disappointed">>
Coach Sharma: No proper footwork, grip is completely wrong.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Your stance leaves you vulnerable to specific types of delivery.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But I did hit several boundaries, sir!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Overjoyed">>
Raju: And I read your bowling better than I expected!

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Boundaries mean nothing without consistency, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: What matters is whether you can build a foundation of reliable technique.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: On top of whatever natural ability you possess.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Quizzical">>
Coach Sharma: But... there is something there.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Smiling">>
Coach Sharma: Something authentic.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Proud">>
Coach Sharma: You have natural timing, hand-eye coordination.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Smiling">>
Coach Sharma: And the kind of cricket instincts that can't be purchased or trained into someone.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Can you teach me proper technique, sir?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: Can you help me build on whatever natural ability I have?

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Teaching at this level costs serious money, boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Serious">>
Coach Sharma: Money for equipment, facility time, individual instruction, structured progression.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachSharma" "Disappointed">>
Coach Sharma: Money that I know you and your family don't have.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju absorbs the reality, the familiar weight returns.

His demonstrated talent and proven character still cannot overcome the economic barriers.

The system measures potential in rupees rather than ability.

Yet his brief taste of proper cricket assessment has revealed both the extent of his natural gifts and the magnitude of what proper coaching might achieve.

A burning awareness of possibilities that remain tantalizingly out of reach.

<<set $CoachSharma_Day = 5>>
<<EndEvent true>>
